{
  "ref": "3-005",
  "proposal": "review/3-005/proposal.json",
  "saved_at": "2026-07-30T20:32:26-0400",
  "lines": {
    "0": {
      "text": "Wuˊthɪtčä-čaˊkêt-tɵˊmg̣ɪn (“middle sister-mate”)",
      "edited": true
    },
    "1": {
      "text": "Middle sister (said by female).",
      "edited": false
    },
    "2": {
      "text": "Ñêˊnča-čaˊkêt-tɵˊmg̣ɪn (“younger sister-mate”).",
      "edited": true
    },
    "3": {
      "text": "Younger sister (said by female).",
      "edited": false
    },
    "4": {
      "text": "Yêᵋˊlhɪ-tɵˊmg̣ɪn (“cousin-mate”), more rarely",
      "edited": true
    },
    "5": {
      "text": "Yêᵋˊlo",
      "edited": true
    },
    "6": {
      "text": "Male cousin, paternal and maternal.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "7": {
      "text": "Ñaw-yêᵋˊlhɪ-tɵˊmg̣ɪn (in respect to male cousins)¹",
      "edited": true
    },
    "8": {
      "text": "Female cousin, paternal and maternal.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "9": {
      "text": "Eˊkɪk",
      "edited": true
    },
    "10": {
      "text": "Son.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "11": {
      "text": "Ñeˊekɪk",
      "edited": true
    },
    "12": {
      "text": "Daughter.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "13": {
      "text": "ᴇʟuˊê (pl. ᴇʟuˊwg̣ot)",
      "edited": true
    },
    "14": {
      "text": "Grandson and nephew.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "15": {
      "text": "Ñauʟuˊê",
      "edited": true
    },
    "16": {
      "text": "Grand-daughter and niece.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "17": {
      "text": "ᴇʟoˊo-tɵˊmg̣ɪn ²",
      "edited": true
    },
    "18": {
      "text": "Parents’ cousin’s son.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "19": {
      "text": "Ñauʟoˊo-tɵˊmg̣ɪn ³",
      "edited": true
    },
    "20": {
      "text": "Parents’ cousin’s daughter.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "21": {
      "text": "BOGORAS, THE CHUKCHEE.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "22": {
      "text": "Of all these terms, a collective may be formed by means of the word",
      "edited": false
    },
    "23": {
      "text": "-ret, -rat, which signifies “collection,” “set,” and is used only in combination",
      "edited": false
    },
    "24": {
      "text": "with others. Thus, yičemreˊt, “company of brothers;” čakêˊttɪrat, “company",
      "edited": false
    },
    "25": {
      "text": "of sisters” (in regard to the male relatives); yêᵋˊlhɪrat, “company of male",
      "edited": false
    },
    "26": {
      "text": "cousins;” kret, “company of boys” (k shortened for kmiˊñin, “boy,” “child”).",
      "edited": false
    },
    "27": {
      "text": "The fourth degree of relationship is designated by means of the stem",
      "edited": false
    },
    "28": {
      "text": "yɪˊlhɪ, which signifies “link,” “junction.” Thus, yɪˊlhɪ-miˊrg̣ɪn, “great-grandfather;”",
      "edited": false
    },
    "29": {
      "text": "yɪlh-ᴇʟuˊê, “great-grandson;” yɪlhɪʟoˊo-tɵˊmg̣ɪn, “male cousin twice removed,” etc.",
      "edited": true
    },
    "30": {
      "text": "The more remote degrees of relationship are designated as čɪmčeˊkin,",
      "edited": false
    },
    "31": {
      "text": "“the near one;” or čičeˊtkin, čičeˊʟeñ, “kinsman.” The compass of the second",
      "edited": false
    },
    "32": {
      "text": "term is larger than that of the first.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "33": {
      "text": "All degrees of step-relations are designated with the suffix -lqäl, meaning",
      "edited": false
    },
    "34": {
      "text": "“intended for.”⁴ Thus ᴇʟɪˊhɪlqäl, “step-father;” ᴇʟaˊlqäl, “step-mother,” also,",
      "edited": false
    },
    "35": {
      "text": "in polygamous families, “another wife of my father;” eˊkkelqäl, “step-son;”",
      "edited": false
    },
    "36": {
      "text": "ñeeˊkkelqäl, “step-daughter;” yiˊčemit-tuˊmg̣älqäl, “step-brother;” čakêˊttɪlqäl,",
      "edited": true
    },
    "37": {
      "text": "“step-sister” (in respect to the brother), etc. Even ñew-miˊrg̣ɪlqäl, “step-grand-",
      "edited": false
    },
    "38": {
      "text": "mother,” is often used in polygamous families.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "39": {
      "text": "539",
      "edited": false
    },
    "40": {
      "text": "Affinity is designated as follows: —",
      "edited": false
    },
    "41": {
      "text": "Father-in-law.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "42": {
      "text": "Mataˊlɪn ⁵",
      "edited": true
    },
    "43": {
      "text": "Ñaw-mataˊlɪn",
      "edited": true
    },
    "44": {
      "text": "Mother-in-law.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "45": {
      "text": "Son-in-law.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "46": {
      "text": "ɪntuˊulpᴇrⁱ",
      "edited": true
    },
    "47": {
      "text": "Daughter-in-law.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "48": {
      "text": "ɪnteˊ",
      "edited": true
    },
    "49": {
      "text": "Brother-in-law.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "50": {
      "text": "Aačêˊw-mataˊlɪn ⁶",
      "edited": true
    },
    "51": {
      "text": "Ñaučhän-mataˊlɪn ⁶",
      "edited": false
    },
    "52": {
      "text": "Sister-in-law.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "53": {
      "text": "",
      "edited": true
    },
    "54": {
      "text": "Husband of wife’s sister.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "55": {
      "text": "Takaˊlhɪn",
      "edited": true
    },
    "56": {
      "text": "Son-in-law’s or daughter-in-law’s father.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "57": {
      "text": "Umiˊrit",
      "edited": true
    },
    "58": {
      "text": "Son-in-law’s or daughter-in-law’s mother.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "59": {
      "text": "Ñeumiˊrit (“woman umiˊrit”)",
      "edited": true
    },
    "60": {
      "text": "¹ Women use the term ñawˊg̣êl, which is the female pronunciation of ñaw-yêᵋˊlhɪ.",
      "edited": false
    },
    "61": {
      "text": "² Female pronunciation, ᴇʟuˊwg̣o-tɵˊmg̣ɪn. ᴇʟoo and ᴇʟuˊe are related.",
      "edited": true
    },
    "62": {
      "text": "³ Female pronunciation, ñauʟuˊwg̣o-tɵˊmg̣ɪn. Women among themselves use simply the term ñawˊg̣êl.",
      "edited": true
    },
    "63": {
      "text": "⁴ For instance, uwäˊᵋqučilqäl (“intended for husband”), “bridegroom;” ñeˊwänlɪqäl (“intended for wife”), “bride.”",
      "edited": false
    },
    "64": {
      "text": "⁵ From the verb mataˊrkɪn (“thou takest,” “thou takest to wife”).",
      "edited": false
    },
    "65": {
      "text": "⁶ Aaˊčêk means “young man;” ñeˊus˙qät means “woman.” These terms are used by both wedded parties.",
      "edited": true
    },
    "66": {
      "text": "Sometimes they say also ᴇndêw-mataˊlɪn (“wife’s uncle”) and ᴇččaiˊñaw-mataˊlɪn (“wife’s aunt”).",
      "edited": true
    }
  }
}
